   The 'B' at index 5 is not covered.
   Count = 1.
2. Next 'B' is at index 5.
   We apply operation on range $[5, 5+3-1] = [5, 7]$.
   Since the string length is 6, the range is effectively $[5, 5]$.
   This covers index 5.
   Count = 2.
   All 'B's covered.
   Result: 2.
